# Web app

- React 19, Vite, strict TypeScript. The web app is both a full player and the setup and admin console for the server.
- Organize by feature: `src/features/<feature>/` (home, guide, sports, library, player, settings, setup), shared UI in `src/ui/`, and API access in `src/api/`. Keep files focused; split anything growing past about 300 lines.
- API types come from `api/openapi.yaml` (generated). Don't hand-write response types that already exist in the spec.
- Server state goes through the query layer and the events WebSocket. Don't add ad-hoc polling loops.
- Styling uses the design tokens in `src/theme/tokens.css`, generated from `design/tokens.json`. No raw hex colors or one-off spacing in components.
- Every screen works at three sizes: phone (touch), desktop (mouse and keyboard), and 10-foot TV (arrow-key focus, large type). Focus must always be visible and never lost when content updates.
- Playback uses hls.js with native HLS as the fallback. Live playback respects the sync engine: don't seek or change `playbackRate` directly in a component.
- Accessibility: every control has an accessible name, dialogs trap and return focus, and motion respects `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Code-split by route; keep the initial bundle small.
